From 656837320c548f5ca87cedcf5f94135d2465f4de Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Phil <300208363+calicopizzadelivery@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 18:22:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] One tile per app: skip the phone launcher when there is a TV
 one

Installed apps are gathered from both LEANBACK_LAUNCHER and LAUNCHER
and folded together by the activity each resolves to. That folds an app
whose TV and phone entry points are the same activity, but not one that
has a separate phone activity: Lemuroid showed twice, and its second
tile opened the touch interface. An app's LAUNCHER activity is now left
out when the same package has a LEANBACK_LAUNCHER one. Apps with only a
phone launcher are shown as before.

Change-Id: I5b8e2d4f6a1c3e7b9d0f2a4c6e8b1d3f5a7c9e02
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../org/lineageos/tv/launcher/flow/InstalledAppsFlow.kt    | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/app/src/main/java/org/lineageos/tv/launcher/flow/InstalledAppsFlow.kt b/app/src/main/java/org/lineageos/tv/launcher/flow/InstalledAppsFlow.kt
index a33b158..c5e25c8 100644
--- a/app/src/main/java/org/lineageos/tv/launcher/flow/InstalledAppsFlow.kt
+++ b/app/src/main/java/org/lineageos/tv/launcher/flow/InstalledAppsFlow.kt
@@ -46,10 +46,15 @@ class InstalledAppsFlow(private val context: Context) {
                 .mapNotNull { resolveInfo ->
                     LeanbackAppInfo(resolveInfo, context)
                 }
+        // An app with a TV entry point is shown by that alone. Apps whose TV
+        // and phone launchers are the same activity were already folded
+        // together below; an app that has a separate phone activity (Lemuroid,
+        // for one) otherwise got a second tile opening its touch interface.
+        val leanbackPackages = leanbackLauncherActivities.map { it.packageName }.toSet()
         val launcherActivities =
             packageManager.queryIntentActivities(launcherIntent, 0).mapNotNull { resolveInfo ->
                 AppInfo(resolveInfo, context)
-            }
+            }.filter { it.packageName !in leanbackPackages }
 
         (leanbackLauncherActivities + launcherActivities).distinctBy {
             it.launchIntent?.resolveActivityInfo(
-- 
